<title>GERMANY: Krupp supervisory board to meet Saturday.</title>
<headline>Krupp supervisory board to meet Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German steel maker Fried. Krupp AG planned to hold extraordinary meetings of two supervisory boards on Saturday, sources close to the company said on Friday.</p>
<p>The supervisory board of steel unit Krupp-Hoesch Stahl AG would meet in Essen at 10 a.m., sources said. The parent company supervisory board would meet at 2 p.m., they said.</p>
<p>Krupp, which is negotiating to form a joint steel company with rival Thyssen AG, declined to comment.</p>
<p>The talks got underway on Thursday after Krupp launched a hostile takeover bid for Thyssen.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
